    "title": {
      "en": "Stitches is Currently Neutral, but will Terrorize Duskwood Again Soon in WoW: Forever",
      "es": "Stitches es actualmente neutral, pero volverá a aterrorizar a Duskwood pronto en WoW: Forever"
    },
    "summary": {
      "en": "Stitches is Currently Neutral, but will Terrorize Duskwood Again Soon in WoW: Forever...",
      "es": "Stitches es actualmente neutral, pero volverá a aterrorizar a Duskwood pronto en WoW: Forever..."
    },
    "contentHtml": "\n            <div id=\"news-post-6ac0cc61d04814.36892414\" data-insert-ads=\"article\" data-zaf-dynamic=\"article\" data-units-dynamic=\"article\" data-zaf-slot=\"true\">Stitches is notorious for killing unsuspecting players in Duskwood, but right now, he's a little calmer than normal - Blizzard has confirmed that this is a bug and will be fixed. <br><br>One of the most infamous NPC's in the Eastern Kingdoms, there's no mob quite like Stitches when it comes to striking fear into players' hearts (unless you're talking about Hogger). Since the latest WoW: Forever beta build, though, Stitches has been noticeably... nicer. Instead of being a hostile elite patrolling the zone, Stitches has been spotted in a neutral state, meaning he won't kill unsuspecting passersby like usual. Players have already taken to social media regarding the change, and thankfully, an answer has already been given: Principal Game Designer Johnny Cash has confirmed that <a data-entity=\"npc\" href=\"https://www.wowhead.com/forever/npc=412/stitches\"><span class=\"tinyicontxt\">Stitches</span></a> shouldn't be neutral, and the bug is working on being fixed.<br><br><div class=\"wh-center\" style=\"text-align: -webkit-center;\"><div class=\"markup-bluetweet exclude-units\"><a href=\"https://twitter.com/wowheadtweets/status/2106031126322274580\">Tweet #2106031126322274580</a></div></div><br><br>The terror of Duskwood will be back again soon - until then, players will have to wait for Stitches to return to his old fearsome self!</div>\n            \n            <noscript>Stitches is notorious for killing unsuspecting players in Duskwood, but right now, he's a little calmer than normal - Blizzard has confirmed that this is a bug and will be fixed. <br /><br />One of the most infamous NPC's in the Eastern Kingdoms, there's no mob quite like Stitches when it comes to striking fear into players' hearts (unless you're talking about Hogger). Since the latest WoW: Forever beta build, though, Stitches has been noticeably... nicer. Instead of being a hostile elite patrolling the zone, Stitches has been spotted in a neutral state, meaning he won't kill unsuspecting passersby like usual. Players have already taken to social media regarding the change, and thankfully, an answer has already been given: Principal Game Designer Johnny Cash has confirmed that <a href=\"/forever/npc=412/stitches\">Stitches</a> shouldn't be neutral, and the bug is working on being fixed.<br /><br />The terror of Duskwood will be back again soon - until then, players will have to wait for Stitches to return to his old fearsome self!</noscript>            \n        ",
